From b8261ce10d68d167c4bd7339d4c81c4880a3c241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini stable rebase <stable-rebase@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:52:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] volume object overlap broad phase

Replace repeated all-object/all-volume-object bounds scans with a balanced
conservative broad phase. Leaf tests still call BoundBox::intersects, preserving
its rounded center/size arithmetic rather than substituting endpoint overlap.
Invalid or nonfinite bounds retain the original exact linear predicate. The
existing flag updates, self exclusion and pre-bounds fallback are unchanged.

Rationale: Large instanced scenes repeat quadratic object-volume bounds searches during flag updates even when most candidates are spatially separated.
Contract: Preserve exact overlap results, object identity exclusion, invalid-bound fallback, pre-bounds behavior, packed-bit OR semantics and valid-pass host boolean resets.
Tests: tests/core_object_volume_bounds_smoke.py, scripts/verify-upstream-patches.py

Rebased-From: b2e6b875571979ee570592db50e5a2bde28599db
Previous-Patch: patches/0087-volume-object-overlap-broad-phase.patch
Previous-Patch-SHA256: f4be8f2ad5a02a62e1db421feb97740f4932f9a6e5e29bd1490c7ac277e71957
Rationale: Large instanced scenes repeatedly scan every object against every volume-object bound during flag updates. A conservative spatial broad phase avoids this quadratic search while exact leaves retain the existing rounded center/size predicate.
Contract: Bound object-volume overlap flag queries with a conservative spatial broad phase while retaining exact BoundBox::intersects leaf tests, self exclusion, invalid-bound fallback and the existing packed-flag update semantics.
Tests: tests/core_object_volume_bounds_smoke.py, scripts/verify-upstream-patches.py

